eak holding. However, my opponent has checked through every single round including pre-flop, flop, and turn. This passive behavior strongly indicates weakness. A small bluff of 100 chips could fold out similar weak holdings, but it also risks getting called by any pair or better Ace. Given that checking costs me nothing and gives me a chance to win at showdown if they also have a weak hand, the safest play is to check and see their cards.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
