tentially induce a bluff if opponent is weak\n5. Preserve my chip lead without unnecessary risk\n\nSince I'm ahead in cumulative chips, there's no need to take unnecessary risks with a marginal hand. If my opponent checks back, I can reassess on the turn. If they bet, I can likely fold without significant damage.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
